{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","x":0,"y":-260,"width":440,"height":190,"text":"**Legend**\n🟩 done · 🟨 now · ⬜ not yet · 🟥 not taught · 🟪 self-study · 🟧 shaky (see the ⚠ line)\n⚠ GAP = in the course outline, no STQ question on it\nS6 / S8 / S9 = STQ06 / 08 / 09 question numbers · files in `~/Desktop/fn/`\nCrow updates the colours as blocks close."},
		{"id":"t6s1","type":"text","text":"**Types of assets**\nworking capital vs non-current · permanent vs variable · spontaneous vs non-spontaneous\nS6: Q1, 2, 3, 11\n⚠ GAP: operating vs non-operating assets","x":900,"y":0,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t6s2","type":"text","text":"**Reading the quarters (numbers)**\nWC = current assets · permanent WC = the LOWEST quarter · permanent assets = PWC + net non-CA\nS6: Q14–17","x":900,"y":200,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t6s3","type":"text","text":"**Types of funds**\nshort vs long-term · spontaneous (AP, accruals) vs non-spontaneous (loans)\nS6: Q12\n⚠ GAP: operating vs non-operating ST funds · interest-bearing vs not","x":900,"y":400,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t6s4","type":"text","text":"**Hedging / maturity matching / self-liquidating**\nmatch the fund's life to the asset's life · a gap can still exist (3-month loan vs 6-month AR)\nS6: Q4, 10, 13","x":900,"y":600,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t6s5","type":"text","text":"**Conservative**\nLT funds cover the peaks too · excess cash → marketable securities · lowest return, most expensive\nS6: Q8, 9, 19","x":900,"y":800,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t6s6","type":"text","text":"**Aggressive**\nST funds into permanent WC, even into non-CA · highest return, renewal risk\nS6: Q5, 6, 7, 18, 20","x":900,"y":1000,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t6","type":"text","text":"## 6. Financing Policies\nweek 8 (30 Sep) · STQ06: 20 T/F, key IN the PDF (pp. 3–5)\nPast finals: **0 Qs in either** ⚠ (old syllabus? don't skip, don't overspend)","x":400,"y":510,"width":380,"height":150},
		{"id":"t7s1","type":"text","text":"**Short-term sources**\ntrade credit: free vs costly part, cost of 2/10 net 30 · overdraft · commitment loan + fee · PN cost · BEs / commercial paper · secured by AR or inventory\nvia S8: Q10, 19, 21 · Past: 2019 Q8–12\n⚠ GAP: trade-credit cost + loan types, no STQ","x":900,"y":1320,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t7s2","type":"text","text":"**The bond & debenture zoo**\nincome · zero-coupon · collateral trust · revenue · 1st/2nd mortgage vs subordinated · amortized · serial / sinking fund · PIK · perpetual · hybrid · convertible vs exchangeable · fallen angels · private placement\nPast: 2021 Q4–7 · 2019 Q13–16, 20, 21\n⚠ no STQ","x":900,"y":1520,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t7s3","type":"text","text":"**Preferred, common & warrants**\ncumulative preferred vs bonds (risk to the investor) · who requires the higher return · common-share rights, NVDRs, how shares get issued · warrants vs derivative warrants\nPast: 2021 Q8, 9 · 2019 Q17–19\n⚠ no STQ","x":900,"y":1720,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t7s4","type":"text","text":"**Leasing**\nbuying vs leasing, as a concept\nin the outline, not seen on either past final","x":900,"y":1920,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t7","type":"text","text":"## 7. Short- & Long-Term Sources of Funds\nSELF-STUDY · no STQ07 · 'covered if time permits'\n🚨 Past finals: **6 of 26 (2021) · 14 of 32 (2019)**\nthe biggest hole in the STQs","x":400,"y":1630,"width":380,"height":150,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"t8s1","type":"text","text":"**Component-cost theory**\nwhich costs get (1−T) and why · RE isn't free (opportunity cost) · marginal, not historical · flotation RAISES cost\nS8: Q1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 26","x":900,"y":2240,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s2","type":"text","text":"**Cost of debt kd(1−T)**\nYTM on new debt, net of flotation · semiannual → annual\nS8: Q11 (bonds), 15, 16, 24, 33, 43\n← TVM from M1 runs this","x":900,"y":2440,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s3","type":"text","text":"**Cost of preferred kp**\nDp ÷ net price · NO tax adjustment\nS8: Q14, 25, 27, 34","x":900,"y":2640,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s4","type":"text","text":"**Growth rate g**\nhistorical (D0 vs D−n) · g = b × ROE · ROE via Du Pont\nS8: Q18, 41, 42, 45, 52\n← M1 topic 4 (Du Pont) comes back here","x":900,"y":2840,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s5","type":"text","text":"**Cost of RE ks · new common ke**\nks = D1/P0 + g · ke = D1/[P0(1−F)] + g · so ks < ke\nS8: Q11, 13, 35, 44\n⚠ GAP: bond-yield-plus-risk-premium approach (in the outline, no STQ)","x":900,"y":3040,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s6","type":"text","text":"**Short-term debt in the WACC**\nBEs sold at a discount + flotation · simple annual rate · after-tax\nS8: Q19, 21 · ST loans in the mix: Q20, 22","x":900,"y":3240,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s7","type":"text","text":"**WACC & weights**\ntarget/optimal structure · market value over book · which funds count\nS8: Q3, 8, 10, 11, 23","x":900,"y":3440,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s8","type":"text","text":"**MCC schedule & break points** ← the core\nBP = ΔRE ÷ w(equity), or cheap-tranche limit ÷ its weight · one step per BP · run it backwards: weights from an MCC\nS8: Q11, 12, 17, 20, 22, 23, 28, 29–32, 37, 39–40, 47–51","x":900,"y":3640,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s9","type":"text","text":"**Risk-adjusted cost of capital**\none WACC for every project → accepts risky ones, rejects safe ones\nS8: Q3①, Q7③","x":900,"y":3840,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8s10","type":"text","text":"**Capital structure & firm value (trade-off model)**\nWACC U-curve · optimal = min WACC = max share price (NOT book value) · what lowers leverage\nS8: Q36, 38, 46","x":900,"y":4040,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t8","type":"text","text":"## 8. Capital Structure & Cost of Capital\nweeks 9–11 (7, 14, 21 Oct) · STQ08: 52 Qs, solutions xlsx\nPast finals: 2021 Q2, 17–21 · 2019 Q4, 27–32","x":400,"y":3150,"width":380,"height":150},
		{"id":"t9s1","type":"text","text":"**What makes a good criterion + each one's properties**\nNPV · IRR · MIRR · PI · PBP · DPP: risk, TVM, all cash flows, reinvestment rate, cut-off, value-additivity, multiple answers\nS9: Q1–6","x":900,"y":4360,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t9s2","type":"text","text":"**Computing all six (+ EAA)**\none cash-flow table → every number → accept/reject\nS9: Q11(a), Q12 (two outlays), Q20 (X vs Y)","x":900,"y":4560,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t9s3","type":"text","text":"**NPV = 0 → what follows**\nPI = 1 · IRR = WACC · DPP = the project's life\nS9: Q7","x":900,"y":4760,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t9s4","type":"text","text":"**NPV profiles & conflicts**\nIRR = where it crosses zero · crossover rate · independent vs mutually exclusive · early vs late cash flows\nS9: Q13–19","x":900,"y":4960,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t9s5","type":"text","text":"**Unequal lives**\nreplacement chain · EAA\nS9: Q9, 11(b)\n⚠ GAP: unequal SCALES only shows up in Q9's options","x":900,"y":5160,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t9s6","type":"text","text":"**Optimal budget & capital rationing**\nPI ranks under a budget cap · max total NPV inside the cap\nS9: Q8, 10\n⚠ GAP: 'decisions used in practice', no STQ","x":900,"y":5360,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t9","type":"text","text":"## 9. Capital Budgeting Techniques\nweeks 11–13 (21 Oct · 28 Oct · 4 Nov) · BEING TAUGHT\nSTQ09: 20 Qs, solutions xlsx\nPast finals: 2021 Q1, 22–26 · 2019 Q3, 22–26","x":400,"y":4870,"width":380,"height":150,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"t10s1","type":"text","text":"**Dividend policies**\nstable/predictable · constant payout · low-regular-plus-extras · residual\npreview via S8: Q39–40 (residual), Q41\nPast: 2021 Q10 (what lowers dividends), Q15, Q16 (residual, numbers)","x":900,"y":5680,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t10s2","type":"text","text":"**Procedures & firm value**\ndeclaration → ex-dividend → record → payment · do distributions change value?\nPast: 2021 Q12 (who gets the dividend?)","x":900,"y":5880,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t10s3","type":"text","text":"**Repurchases vs dividends**\nhow buybacks work · the comparison · other factors that shape payouts\nPast: 2021 Q11 (why firms buy back)","x":900,"y":6080,"width":440,"height":170},
		{"id":"t10s4","type":"text","text":"**Stock splits & stock dividends**\nmechanics · why firms do them · effect on shareholder wealth\nPast: 2021 Q13, Q14 (3:2 split vs 50% stock dividend: equity lines)","x":900,"y":6280,"width":440,"height":170},
